id: pm-vcs-bcgs
title: Certify pm-vcs PM CLI SDK 2026.9.29 and committed self-host bundle
description: Pin repository-local PM CLI/SDK to published 2026.9.29 while retaining pm-ops 2026.9.28 and pm-changelog 2026.9.25. Regenerate the committed self-host bundle after source and PM evidence are committed. Verify full release gates and packed npm/Bun behavior. The separate all-source CDC benchmark coverage gap remains pm-vcs-tj07.
type: Chore
status: blocked
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-26T14:12:57.090Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-02T22:08:41.858Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "Installed repository-local PM CLI/SDK equals published 2026.9.29; pm-changelog remains 2026.9.25 and pm-ops remains 2026.9.28; the committed selfhost.bundle tip tree matches the committed source and full release:check passes at the exact candidate head; packed npm/Bun functional VCS acceptance and strict tracker health pass; review, all-source coverage, and full forge/scale limits are stated independently."
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-28T06:20:17.332Z",claude-hub,"2026-09-28: pinned pm-ops 2026.9.28 and re-copied its templates/prepare-merge-driver.ts (pm-ops#124: the omit-dev skip now checks every Node resolution path for an incomplete hoisted pm-ops, so a broken ancestor install fails instead of silently skipping the merge drivers). release:check and changelog:check pass on this branch."
  "2026-10-02T21:43:20.112Z",codex-sol,"Restart audit validates CodeRabbit 4169919316: npm.cmd is not executable via shell-free spawnSync. Add red Windows launch assertion and real Node CLI argv fixture, then pack through npm JS entrypoint on Windows. Preserve shell-free arguments and self-host bundle/HEAD equality."
  "2026-10-02T21:44:53.397Z",codex-sol,Windows launcher assertion fails against npm.cmd and passes using process.execPath. Added real shell-free Node subprocess fixture verifying a spaced npm entrypoint and destination containing ampersand/percent remain literal argv; fallback entrypoint and POSIX args are covered. Focused PM-linked tests pass. Full locked release gate follows at committed self-host head; all-source CDC scope remains pm-vcs-tj07.
  "2026-10-02T22:08:41.858Z",codex-sol,"Full locked release:check passed at implementation head 603d4e2: 793/793 tests, 0 skipped, configured c8 100/100/100/100, lint/typecheck/docstrings/jscpd, real packed native TOON/stat-cache acceptance, committed self-host equality, production audit, identity audit, pack/changelog/attestation/date gates. Scoped PM-linked launcher regression passes. Record this receipt with a regenerated bundle and verify final HEAD self-host equality/strict health. Existing all-source CDC coverage pm-vcs-tj07 and missing substantive configured reviews remain blockers; historical split-commit bundle concern remains the previously accepted refusal."
notes[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-26T14:24:18.713Z","harness:codex","author=codex,text=Installed @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.9.26, pm-changelog 2026.9.25, pm-ops 2026.9.26. Copied the exact pm-ops canonical prepare launcher; regenerated committed selfhost.bundle. Full release:check passed 789/789 tests, 0 skipped, c8 100/100/100/100, native TOON and strace acceptance, self-host source identity, zero production audit findings, npm pack dry run, changelog and attestation gates. Strict PM health passed with an existing advisory provenance warning."
  "2026-09-29T13:24:09.460Z",codex,"Fresh npm/npx and Bun/bunx projects installed packed pm-vcs 2026.7.30 with published CLI 2026.9.29. Both package installs reported copy.complete=true and activated the extension; each initialized native pm-vcs, staged and committed a real text file, then passed strict PM health with zero warnings. This was on the code-identical artifact before the local pin edit; exact new-head full gate and committed self-host bundle revalidation follow."
  "2026-09-29T13:34:25.880Z",codex,"Red-first full release:check on repository-local CLI 2026.9.29 failed the real native TOON and stat-cache installed-CLI tests: both still installed the whole checkout, which the CLI now refuses at its 10000-entry incomplete-source scan boundary. This is a package harness issue, not an upstream CLI defect. Replaced both with a shared npm-pack archive installer that fails closed on pack errors and invalid archive receipts; focused real process tests pass 14/14 with zero skips. CodeRabbit on prior head also identified an existing pm-ops directory without package.json not covered by tests; added that real fixture and verified fail-closed behavior. Full gate and committed self-host bundle revalidation follow."
  "2026-09-29T13:41:48.278Z",codex,"The first fixed-head full gate passed 791/791 tests with zero skips, but its 100% branch threshold correctly found one uncovered platform arm in the new npm launcher selection. Extracted the cross-platform executable choice for direct behavior testing; focused quality-scripts suite now passes 8/8 including both Windows and POSIX launcher names, real packed installs, and failure paths. The previous full run reached no later release gates after this coverage failure. Regenerate committed self-host bundle and rerun full gate before push."
  "2026-09-29T13:47:21.109Z","harness:codex","2026-09-29 exact implementation head 721a025: direct npm run release:check passed with 792/792 tests, zero failures or skips, configured c8 100.00% statements/branches/functions/lines, zero jscpd clones, native TOON, installed-CLI stat-cache strace, self-host tip equality, zero production audit findings, pack dry run, changelog and publish-attestation gates. Installed acceptance now uses a packed archive because CLI 2026.9.29 fails closed on the 10,000-entry whole-checkout scan; focused PM test passed. Fresh npm/npx and Bun/bunx projects installed the packed candidate on published CLI 2026.9.29, committed a real file, and passed strict PM health. Remaining: cdc-benchmark.ts remains outside c8 scope under pm-vcs-tj07; exact remote CI and substantive bot review pending; older PR commit 0467a80 still has a separate bundle commit and is not claimed fixed."
files[5]{path,scope,note}:
